  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::26251",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine exhibits a strong binding interaction with multiple potassium channel subunits, specifically Kcnc3, Kcna7, and Kcnv2, all of which are involved in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity. This activity is ultimately linked to the participation of Kcng2, suggesting a potential role for Guanidine in modulating potassium channel function through this pathway. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust and reliable interaction, with each pathway providing a distinct but overlapping set of targets involved in the same biological process. The mechanism appears to involve Guanidine binding to potassium channel subunits, which in turn influence the activity of delayed rectifier potassium channels, potentially affecting Kcng2. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Guanidine and Kcng2, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct effect of Guanidine on Kcng2's function.",
